.venv/
__pycache__
.aip_traces/
.pytest_cache/

# Lab 7 DELIBERATE EXCEPTIONS to the defaults above.
#
# .github/ is ordinarily ignored, but the CI regression gate lives there:
# .github/workflows/eval.yml IS the pipeline. Untracked, the gate never runs at
# all, so those negations are load-bearing. `.env` stays ignored.
#
# ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING HERE. In git the LAST matching pattern wins, so a
# negation written above the rule it overrides does nothing at all. These
# negations used to sit at the top of the file, above the `.aip_cache` rules at
# the bottom -- and `git ls-files .github` came back empty because of it. Keep
# every `!` below the rule it negates.
!.aip_cache/
!.github/
!.github/workflows/
!.github/workflows/eval.yml

Test_by_self
.env
corpus_scaled
ans
zip/*

# The response cache is scratch, not a deliverable. scripts/warm_cache.py
# rebuilds it and scripts/prune_cache.py cuts it to the keys offline replay
# reads, but neither belongs in git: the un-pruned calls.sqlite3 is 144 MB and
# GitHub rejects any blob over 100 MB, which is what broke the push.
# .aip_cache/chroma/ is the vector index duplicating data/index/ at 100x the
# size. No sqlite3 under here is tracked.
#
# Consequence worth knowing: labs/lab7/gate.py replays this cache under
# AIP_OFFLINE=1 and raises CacheMiss when it is absent, so the gate only passes
# where warm_cache.py has been run. reports/gate_metrics.json keeps the
# committed numbers.
.aip_cache/chroma/*
.aip_cache/*.sqlite3

# Machine-specific wall clock from the gate. Deliberately untracked: replaying
# the golden set measures this machine's Python, not the system, and it moves
# every run. reports/gate_metrics.json keeps the reproducible metrics only.
reports/gate_timing.local.json